# Wazuh SIEM Detection & Alert Investigation

## Project Overview

This project demonstrates the deployment, monitoring, investigation, and response capabilities of the Wazuh SIEM platform.

The objective was to detect and investigate SSH brute-force activity against a Linux endpoint, analyze alerts using the MITRE ATT&CK framework, and automatically block malicious activity through Wazuh Active Response.

---

## Technologies Used

- Wazuh SIEM
- Ubuntu 20.04.4 LTS
- Linux Security Logs
- MITRE ATT&CK Framework
- Active Response
- Security Configuration Assessment (SCA)
- Security Event Monitoring

---

## Lab Environment

| Component | Description |
|------------|------------|
| SIEM | Wazuh v4.2.5 |
| Endpoint | Ubuntu 20.04.4 LTS |
| Monitoring | Wazuh Agent |
| Attack Type | SSH Brute Force |
| Log Source | /var/log/auth.log |
| MITRE Technique | T1110 - Brute Force |
| MITRE Tactic | Credential Access |

---

## Project Objectives

- Deploy and configure Wazuh agents
- Monitor endpoint activity
- Detect SSH brute-force attacks
- Investigate security alerts
- Analyze events using MITRE ATT&CK
