# Phase 3: Security Event Detection

Wazuh detected multiple failed SSH authentication attempts.

### Security Events

![Security Events](screenshots/03-security-events-rule5710.png)

Detected activity included:

- Invalid usernames
- Failed authentication attempts
- Repeated login attempts

### Alert Details

| Alert Type | Value |
|------------|--------|
| Rule ID | 5710 |
| Severity Level | 5 |
| Log Source | /var/log/auth.log |
| Detection | SSH Authentication Failure |

---

# Phase 4: MITRE ATT&CK Analysis

The detected activity was automatically mapped to the MITRE ATT&CK framework.

### MITRE ATT&CK Dashboard

![MITRE ATT&CK](screenshots/04-mitre-dashboard.png)

### Alert Investigation

![Alert Details](screenshots/05-alert-details.png)

#### Findings

| MITRE Category | Value |
|---------------|--------|
| Technique ID | T1110 |
| Technique | Brute Force |
| Tactic | Credential Access |

This mapping allowed the activity to be classified as a brute-force attack attempting unauthorized access.

---

# Phase 5: Automated Incident Response

Wazuh Active Response was configured to automatically block malicious IP addresses.

### Host Blocked by Active Response

![Active Response](screenshots/06-host-blocked.png)

The response mechanism:

- Detected brute-force activity
- Triggered the firewall-drop action
- Blocked the attacking IP address
- Logged the response event

